course: dictionary
lesson: 9294
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning. The word speaker is one of them. To find the right meaning, look at the words around it, because they are the context and they give clues. «The guest speaker told us how volcanoes form» tells you a speaker is a person giving a talk, because a guest visits to talk to the school.
explain: Now try a different sentence: «Turn the speaker up, the music is too quiet.» Music, turn up and quiet point to a device that makes sound louder, not a person. Always ask: which meaning fits here? Then put that meaning into the sentence in place of the hard word and check it still makes sense.
explain: Some meanings are linked to a place or a topic. In a parliament, «the Speaker» with a capital S is the person who runs the debates. A «native speaker» of a language grew up using it. Clues like parliament, music or grew up tell you which meaning the writer chose.
fact: Speaker has several meanings, so context clues help you choose the right one.
fact: A speaker can be a person who gives a talk to an audience, as in «a guest speaker».
fact: A speaker can be a device that makes sound louder, as in «a Bluetooth speaker» or «a loudspeaker».
fact: A speaker can be a person who speaks a language, as in «a native speaker» of French, and in some parliaments the Speaker is the person in charge of debates.
fact: A good check is to swap your meaning into the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
exercise: «The guest speaker told us how volcanoes form.» What does speaker mean here? | *A person giving a talk to an audience | A device that makes sound louder | A person who speaks a language | The person in charge of a parliament debate
exercise: Priya turned up the speaker so the music filled the whole room. What does speaker mean here? | A talk given in assembly | A person who speaks French | *A device that makes sound louder | A person giving a talk
exercise: «She is a native speaker of Welsh.» What does speaker mean here? | *A person who speaks a language | The Speaker of the parliament | A device that makes sound louder | A person giving a talk
test: In parliament, the Speaker keeps order during debates. What does Speaker mean here? | A person who gives a talk | A person who speaks a language | *The person in charge of debates | A device for playing music
test: Which phrase means a person who has spoken a language since birth? | Guest speaker | *Native speaker | Bluetooth speaker | Loudspeaker
exam: Which sentence uses speaker to mean a person giving a talk? | She is a fluent speaker of Italian and Spanish | *The speaker in assembly was a nurse who told us about her job | Turn the speaker down, please, it is too loud | The speaker crackled when the battery ran low
